<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wareru</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1253">1253</a>–1307</span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wareru was the founder of the Mon kingdom of Martaban, later called Hanthawaddy, in lower <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/burma">Burma</a>. A Mon of humble origin, he seized Martaban in 1287 after the fall of the Pagan Kingdom and gained recognition from King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ram-khamhaeng">Ram Khamhaeng</a> of Sukhothai. He is credited with a code of law, the Wareru Dhammathat, and was assassinated in 1307.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/wareru.jpg" alt="Wareru" width="320" height="427" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Htawmonzel · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wareru.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
